{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggeUVPbw6AervhEqUYh9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This question can't be answered within the ligand-field model, because permanganate is a d⁰ complex.\n\nMn(VII) in MnO₄⁻ has no d electrons, so there are no d–d transitions. A Tanabe–Sugano analysis fits d–d bands to Dq and B, and it needs a d²–d⁸ configuration. For d⁰ there are no ligand-field terms to fit.\n\nThe three bands are also not d–d bands. They are ligand-to-metal charge-transfer (LMCT) transitions, from O 2p-based orbitals to the empty Mn 3d orbitals (e and t₂). The usual assignments are:\n- 17 570 cm⁻¹: ¹A₁ → ¹T₂ (1t₁ → 2e)\n- 31 560 cm⁻¹: ¹A₁ → ¹T₂ (1t₁ → 7t₂), assigned alongside the next band\n- 38 320 cm⁻¹: ¹A₁ → ¹T₂ (6t₂ → 2e)\n\nThe molar absorptivities of about 1 500–3 000 M⁻¹ cm⁻¹ are also much too high for d–d bands. Those are Laporte-forbidden in centrosymmetric complexes and typically have ε below about 100. Even in tetrahedral complexes, where the Laporte rule is relaxed, d–d bands rarely exceed a few hundred.\n\nFitting these bands to Dq and B would give numbers with no physical meaning. The charge-transfer energies depend on ligand orbital energies and metal–ligand covalency. The e–t₂ splitting in a d⁰ ion can be estimated from molecular-orbital calculations, but that is not a Dq/B/C ligand-field parameter set, and Racah B is not defined for a d⁰ ion. I'm therefore not reporting values.\n\n{\"Dq\": null, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": true, \"reason\": \"MnO4- is d0 and its bands are O→Mn charge-transfer, not d-d transitions, so Dq and B cannot be determined from ligand-field theory.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":7806,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"09ea8c5c-0537-4ded-adf4-52ca1cae1cff","uuid":"c6544fe7-2bbe-4902-b989-49256ed284ae","timestamp":"2026-11-03T20:44:35.562Z","request_id":"req_011CggeUV5FRP7feHVxBow1g"}
